XR diorama: spheres kept outside the table (the birds flying around the room)

aurora_xr_set_diorama_free: up to 16 spheres in the table's space whose points the eyes' mask keeps
opaque outside the table (patch 0026's mask), so what flies inside them (the seagulls, the birds) is
seen around the model in the room.

diff --git a/include/aurora/xr.h b/include/aurora/xr.h
--- a/include/aurora/xr.h
+++ b/include/aurora/xr.h
@@ -50,6 +50,11 @@
  * shape is the sphere of radius 1 around the table space's origin, fading over fade[0]. */
 void aurora_xr_set_diorama_mask(const float tableFromHead[12], const float proj[6], float eyeShift,
                                 const float fade[4]);
+/* Patch 0029, from the game thread with the mask: spheres in the table's space (x, y, z, radius each,
+ * up to AURORA_XR_FREE_SPHERES) whose points stay in the picture outside the table (the birds flying
+ * around the room). count 0: none. */
+#define AURORA_XR_FREE_SPHERES 16
+void aurora_xr_set_diorama_free(const float* spheres, int count);
 
 /* Patch 0025, from the game thread while it records a frame: the head pose it is drawn for (a tag
  * the XR layer gave out) and whether it is the diorama. Taken by the frame's present. */
diff --git a/lib/webgpu/xr_present.hpp b/lib/webgpu/xr_present.hpp
--- a/lib/webgpu/xr_present.hpp
+++ b/lib/webgpu/xr_present.hpp
@@ -41,6 +41,8 @@
   float proj[6];           // GXSetProjection's perspective parameters
   float eyeShift;          // b (the right eye's; the left's is -b)
   float fade[4];           // x, z, y in table units; [3] 1 = the bubble (patch 0027)
+  float free[16][4];       // patch 0029: spheres kept outside the table (x, y, z, radius)
+  int freeCount;
 };
 bool diorama_mask(DioramaMask& out) noexcept;
 
